A||||3||MooCow||What would it $ to get the engine rebuild?||||5
Z||000000||MooCow||11-29-1999||09:23 AM||||Can someone give me an estimation of how much it would would cost if I found a mechanic to rebuild and 86SE v6 Fiero??  I have $3,500 to spend on a Fiero and any parts I need for it. All information will help me greatly.||||reg||5
Z||000001||2FAST4U||11-29-1999||10:55 PM||||If you are into doing it yourself you can get a complete remanufactured engine from your local chevrolet or Pontiac delear for less than 2,000.<P>If you just want a simple rebuild from a local mechanic expect to pay about 3,000. any performance upgrades will raise the price accordingly.<P>Because of the cost I would not recommend having a auto dealership shop do the work. All dealership shops charge according to an hourly schedule listed in a book. If the book says that that a job should take 3 hours thats what you are charged even if it only takes 30 minutes to complete the job. A lot of regular shops are billing this way now so shop around but mack sure you find a reputable shop. I have found that hhe smaller shops are the best way to go. Ask questions, ask frinds, check references, check with the BBB. A poor quality rebuild from a less than reputable shop will cost more in lost time and headaches than any amount of money could pay for. Get a good waranty / garantee and cost estimate BEFORE you agree to anything and GET IT IN WRITING!<P>Good Luck||||reg||1
Z||000002||turbo86se||11-29-1999||11:22 PM||||MooCow, For less than $3500, my mechanic and friend will install a 3800 in your 86SE. You'll have money left over for the brake and suspension upgrades you'll need to compensate for the additional power. All you need to do is get it to Myrtle Beach SC, we'll supply the engine and parts....||||reg||1
Z||000003||dogtired||11-30-1999||09:08 AM||||SHOP AROUND<BR>The more work you will do will usually make it cost less. I removed and reinstalled my V6, once it was out I sent it to a great local machine shop. $1000. later I had a new rebuilt motor delivered to me. He even long blocked it so all I had to do was bolt it back in the car. Its great to have a friend with a machine shop, that does quality work, that you can trust.. But be very careful, there are alot more machine shops out there that just want to get in your pocket.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Now if you are looking for Hi-Pro and trick parts the price will go up very quickly.<BR>PROCEED WITH CAUTION!||||reg||10
